# --- Raw data is immutable and NOT versioned here (size + license) ---
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/raw/README.md

# Derived data: cleaned CSVs are reproducible from raw + config -> not committed
data/cleaned/*
!data/cleaned/.gitkeep

# --- The RAG index (S4.1) is a build artifact, not a record ---
# 4.7 MB of Chroma SQLite, fully regenerable from data/cleaned + the frozen
# split + configs/s4_index.yaml. Committing it would put a binary blob in the
# history that no reviewer can read and no diff can check.
#
# What IS committed is the evidence about it: results/s4_index_manifest.json
# carries the row count, the axis-level counts, and a SHA-256 digest over the
# sorted review_ids. A rebuild claiming to be identical is checked against that
# digest rather than believed -- which is strictly better than storing the blob,
# because the digest is human-readable and the blob is not.
data/rag/

# !!! EXCEPTION: plot synopses ARE committed. They are hand-collected primary
# data -- no script can regenerate them, and re-collecting means re-reading the
# sources by hand. They are also the only held-out element of the evaluation, so
# losing them invalidates S6. Treat them like the split map, not like a cache.
!data/plots/
!data/plots/*.csv

# !!! EXCEPTION: split map IS committed. It is the single most important
# artifact of the thesis (see pipeline section A). Never gitignore it.
!data/splits/
!data/splits/*.json

# Env / caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.env
wandb/
*.pt
*.bin
.DS_Store

# Unzipped Kaggle output bundles -- transient, the files inside are what matter
zip/
*.zip

# Raw harvest -- regenerable by re-running plots_scrape.py; only the sampled
# 130 in plots_bn.csv are committed.
data/plots/plots_bn_harvest.csv
data/plots/.harvest_state.json
data/plots/review.html

# Annotation sheets carry 300 rows of the licensed corpus and are regenerable
# from the frozen split + seed 42, so they are NOT committed -- same reason as
# data/cleaned/. The RATINGS are regenerable by nothing, so g300_score.py
# extracts them text-free to results/g300_ratings.csv, which IS committed.
data/annotation/*.csv
data/annotation/*.xlsx
data/annotation/intrusion/*.csv
results/_dryrun/

# --- Trained artifacts (S3.3) ---
# The two small joblibs ARE committed: verifier_a.joblib is the in-loop
# verifier itself (logistic coefficients, 15K) and losing it means the S3.2b
# number cannot be re-checked against the object that produced it.
# The BanglaBERT checkpoint dir is 424M and is NOT committed -- it is
# reproducible from configs/s3d_verifier_b.yaml + seed 42, and a 424M blob in
# a thesis repo is a mistake that cannot be undone by a later commit.
artifacts/verifier_b/

# --- Rule-7 PILOT artifacts are NOT committed, on purpose ---
# The IDF-enabled symbolic scorer is a pilot object: rule 7 permits it as an
# explicitly-labelled cheap proxy and NEVER in a result. A committed pilot
# artifact is a file a future session can load by path without ever seeing the
# banner that explains what it is -- so it does not travel with the repo.
# Regenerable from configs/s35_symbolic_pilot_idf.yaml in one command.
artifacts/pilot_*
